in N-free medium containing 0.5 % (w/v) sucrose. After 48 h of N starvation, cultures were split into two shake flasks, and 1 mM KNO3 was added to one while the other served as N-starvation control. For the TurboID cultures, 50 uM biotin was added 48 h after N starvation, and cells were grown further for 15 min or 1\xa0h with or without KNO3. Cells were harvested through vacuum infiltration, sampling 7,5 gram of PSB-D cells for triplicate AP-MS experiments, or 9 grams of PSB-D cells for triplicate PL-MS experiments, and harvested cell material was frozen in N2 and stored at -70°C. Isolation of Protein Complexes by GSrhino-Based Affinity Purification GSrhino-based affinity purification (AP) experiments were performed in triplicate starting from 2.5 g of frozen cell material per replicate (Van Leene et al., 2019). Briefly, protein complexes were trapped through the Protein G part of the GSrhino tag by incubating 25 mg total protein extract per replicate for 45 min with 50 uL in-house prepared magnetic immunoglobulin G (IgG) bead suspension. Beads were washed three times with 500 uL extraction buffer, once with 500 uL extraction buffer without detergent, and once with 800 uL 50 mM NH4HCO3 (pH 8.0). The wash buffer was removed and beads were incubated in 50 uL 50 mM NH4HCO3 supplemented with 1 g Trypsin/Lys-C (Promega) for 4 h at 37°C. Next, the digest was separated from the beads and further incubated overnight with 0.5 g Trypsin/Lys-C at 37°C. Finally, the digest was centrifuged at 20,800 rcf for 5 min, and supernatant was dried in a SpeedVac and stored at 20°C until MS analysis.  TurboID-Based Proximity Labeling (PL) Proximity labeling experiments were performed from 3g harvested cell material per replicate, as described in detail for Arabidopsis PSB-D cells (Arora et al., 2020), using denaturing extraction buffer (100 mM Tris-HCl (pH 7.5), 2% (w/v) SDS, 8 M urea) and with the additional acid elution step following the Trypsin/Lys-C digest, as described in (Van Leene